      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Given that  ${a}^{12}=t$ and ${a}^{4}=s$, what is the value of $\\frac{{t}^{3}}{s}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we carry out the substitution\n\n$$\n\\frac{{t}^{3}}{s}=\\frac{{({a}^{12})}^{3}}{{a}^{4}}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule followed by the quotient rule \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{({a}^{12})}^{3}}{{a}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}^{12\\cdot 3}}{{a}^{4}} & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}^{36}}{{a}^{4}} & = \\\\ {a}^{36-4} & = \\\\ {a}^{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
